REMARKS:
051500Z POSITION NEAR 28.8N 133.4E.
05SEP26. TROPICAL DEPRESSION 23W (TWENTYTHREE), LOCATED
APPROXIMATELY 341 NM EAST-NORTHEAST OF KADENA AB, HAS TRACKED
NORTHWESTWARD AT 15 KNOTS OVER THE PAST SIX HOURS. ANIMATED
ENHANCED INFRARED SATELLITE IMAGERY DEPICTS TROPICAL DEPRESSION
23W WITH AN SMALL AND FULLY-EXPOSED LOW-LEVEL CIRCULATION CENTER
(LLCC). A 051216Z METOP-B ASCAT PASS REVEALED THAT THE WESTERN SIDE
OF THE CIRCULATION HAS STARTED TO UNRAVEL WITH NO CLEAR NORTHERLIES
WRAPPING INTO THE CENTER. THE ASCAT ALSO SHOWED A SMALL PATCH OF
25 KT WINDS IN THE NORTHERN SEMICIRCLE, SUPPORTING THE ASSESSMENT
OF THE INITAL INTENSITY. 23W IS FORECAST TO CONTINUE TRACKING
NORTHWESTWARD TOWARD SOUTHERN KYUSHU AS IT WASHES OUT WITHIN THE
LARGER-SCALE LOW-LEVEL CYCLONIC FLOW OVER THE NEXT 12-24 HOURS.
THIS IS THE FINAL WARNING ON THIS SYSTEM BY THE JOINT TYPHOON
WRNCEN PEARL HARBOR HI. THE SYSTEM WILL BE CLOSELY MONITORED FOR
SIGNS OF REGENERATION. MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE AT 051200Z IS 998
MB. MAXIMUM SIGNIFICANT WAVE HEIGHT AT 051200Z IS 12 FEET.
FOR SIX-HOURLY UPDATES.//
